+{"type":"message","id":"64a48733","parentId":"77a761e6","timestamp":"2026-03-21T20:06:07.179Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Parent conversation handoff summary:\nParent conversation handoff summary\nSummary model: openai-codex/gpt-5.4-mini\nSource items: 79\n\nOverview:\nParent conversation focused on assessing remaining gaps in the Support Bundle Investigator repo against the hiring PDF and PRD v2, after a large Phase 7 implementation landed. The repo already appears to satisfy most core product requirements (CLI-first, local-first, evidence-backed diagnosis, heuristic + AI paths, Markdown/HTML/JSON output, traceability, seeded scenarios), so follow-on work should prioritize reviewer confidence, stronger evals, observability, robustness, and documentation consistency rather than core feature completion.\n\nSettled decisions:\n- The project is effectively past core feature completeness; the remaining work is mainly proof, polish, and confidence-building.\n- The strongest next step is to build a more explicit eval matrix covering scenario, expected top diagnosis, evidence, confidence band, heuristic vs AI results, and spec recommendations.\n- AI-mode behavior is valuable but needs reproducible regression proof via recorded/replayed cassettes or a canonical AI eval corpus.\n- Documentation should be cleaned up so current-complete state is not contradicted by stale roadmap/gap docs.\n- Privacy/sensitive-data assurance should be treated as a differentiating trust feature and validated with tests, especially around secret handling and redaction guidance.\n\nConstraints / must-remember items:\n- README/visible repo surface should make completion obvious; a demo video link is considered a key missing deliverable.\n- Current golden/e2e coverage is narrower than the feature set; several capabilities are unit-tested but under-demonstrated in scenario/e2e form.\n- Observability is currently coarse and should be extended to include retrieval break